[dispensing_by_facility] Dispensing by Facility — Dispensing totals compared across all facilities — KISUMU, KAKAMEGA, LODWAR, TENRI. Use when asked to compare facilities, see which hospital dispenses more, or get a multi-site dispensing breakdown.
[dispensing_by_product] Dispensing by Product — Drug dispensing broken down by canonical product name and therapeutic class. Use when asked about top drugs dispensed, drug consumption by category, which medications are used most, or therapeutic class breakdown.
[dispensing_stockouts] Dispensing Stockouts — Stockout events during dispensing — when stock hit zero or was already negative before dispense. Use when asked about stockouts, drug shortages, out-of-stock events, negative stock, stock availability problems, or stock-out rate.
[dispensing_stock_on_hand] Stock on Hand (Post-Dispense) — Average and minimum stock on hand after dispensing events. Use when asked about remaining stock levels, closing stock, SOH, or inventory levels after dispensing.
[dispensing_financials] Dispensing Financials — Financial summary of dispensing — total drug cost, average unit price, and total discounts applied. Use when asked about pharmacy revenue, cost of drugs dispensed, average drug price, or dispensing discounts.
[patient_dispensing_visits] Patient Dispensing Visits — Pharmacy visits per patient — total visits, distinct patients, drug cost, and average drugs per visit. Use when asked about pharmacy patient counts, how many patients visited pharmacy, dispensing visits, or medication cost per patient.
[arv_dispensing] ARV Dispensing — Visits where antiretrovirals (ARVs) were dispensed. Use when asked about ARV dispensing, HIV medication, antiretroviral volumes, or ART patients receiving medication.
[antibiotic_dispensing] Antibiotic Dispensing — Visits where antibiotics were dispensed, including reserve/last-resort antibiotics (carbapenems, linezolid). Use when asked about antibiotic use, antimicrobial dispensing, AMR-related prescribing, or reserve antibiotic volumes.
[dispensing_by_therapeutic_category] Dispensing by Therapeutic Category — Breakdown of visits by drug category — ARVs, antibiotics, antimalarials, chronic disease drugs (diabetes/cardiovascular), opioids, obstetric drugs. Use when asked about category-level drug dispensing, disease-specific medication volumes, or therapeutic class prescription counts.
[unclassified_drugs] Unclassified Drugs in Dispensing — Count of dispensed drugs with no INN mapping or therapeutic classification. Use when asked about data quality in pharmacy, unmapped drugs, missing drug classifications, or gaps in the product taxonomy.
[product_catalog_summary] Product Catalog Summary — Summary of canonical drug product mappings — total products, unmapped products, and average mapping confidence. Use when asked about the drug formulary, product catalog coverage, INN mapping quality, or how many drugs are in the system.
[products_by_therapeutic_class] Products by Therapeutic Class — Drug products grouped by therapeutic class and subclass. Use when asked about how many drugs are in each therapeutic class, drug catalog breakdown, or formulary composition by category.
[invoice_count] Invoice Count and Payable Amount — Total number of invoices and total payable amount. Use when asked about invoice volumes, number of bills raised, billing activity, total invoiced amounts, or financial billing summary.
[invoices_by_type] Invoices by Type/Status — Invoice count and payable amount broken down by type status. Use when asked about invoice breakdown by type, billing categories, or invoice type analysis.
[invoices_by_patient] Invoices by Patient — Invoice records with patient name and number. Use when asked about patient billing, which patients have invoices, or patient-level invoice lookup.
