[dispensing_financials] Dispensing Financials — Financial breakdown of dispensing — line total, event total, unit price, and discounts. Use when asked about cost of drugs dispensed, dispensing spend, pharmacy revenue, average unit price, or discount amounts.
[dispensing_stockouts] Dispensing Stockouts — Dispense events where stock hit zero (is_stockout_dispense = true). Use when asked about stockouts, drug shortages, out-of-stock dispensing, or how often dispensing caused a stockout at a facility.
[dispensing_negative_stock] Dispensing from Negative Stock — Dispenses made when stock was already negative before the event. More severe than a regular stockout — indicates IOUs to patients or data entry errors. Use when asked about negative stock dispensing, dispensing programme alerts, or critical inventory issues.
[dispensing_trends] Dispensing Trends by Drug — Dispensing counts and value broken down by canonical drug name, therapeutic class, and facility over time. Use when asked about top dispensed drugs, drug consumption trends, dispensing by therapeutic class, or which medicines are used most at a facility.
[patient_dispensing_summary] Patient Dispensing Summary — Per-visit dispensing summary — visit count, distinct patients, total drug cost, drugs per visit, and unclassified drug count. Use when asked about how many patients received medication, pharmacy visit volumes, drug cost per patient, or unclassified drugs dispensed.
[stock_status] Current Stock Status — Current stock status per drug and facility — in stock, low stock, or out of stock. Use when asked about current stock levels, which drugs are out of stock, stock availability, or inventory status by facility or therapeutic class.
[stockout_alerts] Stockout Alerts — Active stockout alerts by drug, facility, and clinical priority. Use when asked about current stockouts, which drugs have stockout alerts, critical drug shortages, or stockout history by first/last occurrence.
[dos_watchlist] Days of Stock Watchlist — Drugs flagged on the days-of-stock watchlist with reorder urgency. Use when asked about drugs running low, reorder alerts, days of stock remaining, urgency of restocking, or which drugs need redistribution.
[drug_redistribution] Drug Redistribution Recommendations — Suggested stock transfers between facilities — surplus facility, deficit facility, drug name, and transfer quantity. Use when asked about inter-facility stock transfers, redistribution recommendations, which facility has surplus/deficit, or drug rebalancing across sites.
[drug_catalog_count] Drug Catalog Size — Total number of canonical drugs in the formulary. Use when asked about how many drugs are in the system, formulary size, or total products.
[drug_taxonomy_lookup] Drug Taxonomy Lookup — Look up a drug by INN or canonical name to get its therapeutic class, subclass, strength, and form. Use when asked about a specific drug's classification, what category a medicine belongs to, or drug reference information.
[product_taxonomy_by_facility] Product Taxonomy by Facility — Drug product mapping quality and coverage per facility — total products, duplicate counts, map status, and match type. Use when asked about drug catalogue coverage at a facility, unmapped products, INN mapping quality, or product taxonomy data completeness.
[inpatient_admissions] Inpatient Admissions — Count of inpatient admissions and total visit count by facility and sex. Use when asked about admissions, hospitalizations, inpatient volume, patients admitted, or bed demand by gender.
[bed_occupancy] Bed Occupancy — Bed occupancy counts and average admission cost by facility, ward category, ward name, and age group. Use when asked about bed occupancy, ward utilisation, inpatient ward load, or admission costs by ward.
[admissions_profile] Admissions Profile — Detailed admission profile — admission type, payment mode, sex, cost, and open admission status. Use when asked about admission demographics, private vs public admissions, payment mode for inpatients, admission costs, or currently open admissions.
[readmissions] Readmissions — Readmission counts and 30-day readmission approximations by facility, ward category, payment mode, and discharge type. Use when asked about readmissions, patients returning within 30 days, discharge outcomes, or readmission rates.
[specialty_admissions] Specialty Admissions — Admissions broken down by specialty ward, payment mode, and facility. Use when asked about admissions by specialty, which wards admit the most patients, specialty utilisation, or ward-level admission breakdown.
[finance_events] Patient Finance Events — Financial events (payments, invoices, credits) by event type, payment mode, and facility. Use when asked about revenue collected, payment events, collections by payment method, cash vs insurance payments, or financial transaction volumes.
[procedure_revenue] Procedure Revenue — Revenue from procedures broken down by revenue category, payment mode, insurer, and facility. Use when asked about procedure revenue, income by service category, revenue by payment mode, or insurer-based billing.
[patient_invoices] Patient Invoice Summary — Patient invoice counts and event counts by facility. Use when asked about invoices raised, billing volumes, number of invoiced patients, or invoice event activity.
[ar_aging] Accounts Receivable Aging — Outstanding receivables grouped by aging bucket, facility, and insurer. Use when asked about AR aging, overdue invoices, how long invoices have been outstanding, accounts receivable breakdown, or insurer debt aging.
[insurance_ar] Insurance Accounts Receivable — Insurance AR by insurer and facility. Use when asked about insurance debt, outstanding insurance claims, which insurer owes the most, or NHIF/corporate receivables.
[disease_burden] Disease Burden — Disease signal counts and prescription counts by disease group and facility. Use when asked about disease burden, common diagnoses, top conditions treated, disease trends, or illness patterns at a facility.
