[canonical_product_taxonomy_count_metrics] Canonical Product Taxonomy Count Metrics — This metric measures the total count of canonical products and the count of duplicate facilities associated with them. Use this metric to analyze product taxonomy data, identify trends in product categorization, and assess the integrity of facility data. Example questions include 'How many unique canonical products are there?' and 'What is the count of duplicate facilities for these products?'
[doctor_note_terms_count] Count of Doctor Note Terms — This metric measures the total count of doctor note terms recorded in the system. It can be used to analyze the frequency of specific terms, clinical syndromes, or disease burden groups in patient notes. Example questions include 'How many times was a specific term used?' or 'What is the distribution of terms by status?'. Consider filtering by clinical syndrome or status for more targeted insights.
[fact_dispensing_metrics] Dispensing Metrics Overview — This metric provides insights into the dispensing activities within the hospital, including total counts, discounts applied, and line totals. Use this metric to analyze dispensing trends, identify stockout events, and evaluate financial impacts. Example questions include 'What is the total number of dispenses this month?' and 'How much discount was given on dispenses last quarter?'
[inpatient_admissions_metrics] Inpatient Admissions Metrics — This metric tracks the total number of inpatient admissions and the total visits count within the hospital system. Use this metric to analyze trends in patient admissions over time, assess the impact of various factors such as patient demographics and admission sources. Example questions include 'How many inpatient admissions were there last month?' or 'What is the total visit count for male patients this year?'
[patient_dispensing_metrics] Patient Dispensing Metrics — This metric tracks the dispensing of medications to patients, including the total number of drugs dispensed, the total cost of drugs, and counts of unclassified drugs. Use this metric to analyze medication distribution trends over time, assess costs, and identify dispensing patterns. Example questions include 'How many drugs were dispensed last month?' or 'What was the total drug cost for a specific facility?'
[patient_finance_event_metrics] Patient Finance Event Metrics — This metric tracks the count and total amount of financial events related to patients, such as payments and invoices. Use it to analyze financial performance, understand payment trends, and assess the impact of different payment modes. Example questions include 'How many finance events occurred last month?' and 'What was the total amount collected from patient payments this quarter?'
[patient_invoice_counts] Patient Invoice Counts — This metric measures the total number of patient invoices and the count of events associated with those invoices. Use this metric to analyze billing activity over time, identify trends in patient invoicing, and assess the volume of invoices generated. It can help answer questions like 'How many invoices were generated last month?' or 'What is the event count for invoices at a specific facility?'
[ar_aging_count_by_facility_and_bucket] Accounts Receivable Aging Count — This metric measures the count of accounts receivable aging records, categorized by aging bucket and facility. Use this metric to analyze the distribution of outstanding receivables over time, helping to identify trends in collections and outstanding balances. Example questions include 'How many accounts are overdue by 30 days at each facility?' and 'What is the count of receivables in each aging bucket for the last invoice month?'
[bed_occupancy_metrics] Bed Occupancy Metrics — This metric measures the total count of bed occupancy and the average admission cost across different facilities and wards. Use this to analyze trends in bed usage and associated costs over time. Example questions include 'What is the average admission cost for the pediatric ward this month?' or 'How many beds were occupied in the main facility last month?'
[dialysis_session_count] Dialysis Session Count — This metric measures the total number of dialysis sessions conducted within a specified time frame. It can be used to analyze trends in dialysis treatment over time, assess resource allocation, and identify peak usage periods. Example questions include 'How many dialysis sessions were held last month?' or 'What is the session count by facility for the past year?'
[disease_burden_metrics] Disease Burden Metrics — This metric tracks the count of diseases and the number of prescriptions associated with each disease group across different facilities. Use this metric to analyze trends in disease prevalence and treatment over time. Example questions include 'What is the total disease count for each facility this month?' and 'How many prescriptions were issued for each disease group last month?'
[dispensing_trends_metrics] Dispensing Trends Metrics — This metric tracks the count and total value of dispensings over time, providing insights into dispensing trends across different facilities and therapeutic classes. Use this metric to answer questions about how dispensing behaviors change month over month, which facilities have the highest dispensing values, and the impact of therapeutic classes on overall dispensing trends. Important filters include facility and therapeutic class.
[rpt_dos_watchlist_count] Count of Watchlist Items — This metric measures the total count of items on the DOS watchlist, providing insights into inventory management and medication monitoring. Use it to answer questions about the number of items flagged for review, track trends over time, or assess the impact of reorder urgency. Important filters include facility and therapeutic class to narrow down specific areas of concern.
[insurance_ar_count_by_facility] Insurance Accounts Receivable Count by Facility — This metric measures the total count of insurance accounts receivable, segmented by facility and insurer. Use this metric to analyze the volume of outstanding insurance claims over time, helping to answer questions like 'How many accounts receivable do we have for each facility this month?' or 'What is the trend in insurance claims by facility?' Filter by facility or insurer for more granular insights.
[kakamega_population_metrics] Kakamega Population Metrics — This metric tracks the total population and visit counts in the Kakamega region. Use it to analyze trends in population and healthcare visits over time, and to answer questions about facility performance and sub-county demographics. Important filters include facility and sub-county to refine your analysis.
[ward_utilisation_metrics] Ward Utilisation Metrics — This metric measures the count and percentage of total utilisation for wards in the Lodwar facility. Use this to analyze how effectively wards are being utilized over time. Example questions include 'What is the total count of patients in each ward?' and 'What percentage of total capacity is being used in each ward?'.
[procedure_revenue_metrics] Procedure Revenue Metrics — This metric tracks the total count of procedures and the average item amount billed across different facilities and insurers. Use it to analyze revenue trends over time, compare performance by facility, or assess the impact of payment modes. Example questions include 'What is the average revenue per procedure for each facility this month?' and 'How does the revenue from different insurers compare?'
[readmission_metrics] Readmission Metrics — This metric tracks the number of readmissions and approximates the count of readmissions within 30 days of discharge. Use this metric to analyze patient readmission trends, evaluate the effectiveness of discharge planning, and identify facilities with high readmission rates. Example questions include 'What is the readmission rate by facility?' or 'How many patients were readmitted within 30 days?'.
[rpt_redistribution_transfer_metrics] Redistribution Transfer Metrics — This metric tracks the count of redistribution events and the suggested transfer quantities between facilities. Use this to analyze how resources are being allocated, identify deficits and surpluses, and assess clinical priorities. Example questions include 'How many transfers were suggested last month?' and 'What is the total suggested transfer quantity for high-priority cases?'
[specialty_admissions_count] Specialty Admissions Count — This metric measures the total number of specialty admissions to the hospital. It can be used to analyze trends in admissions over time, assess the performance of different facilities, and evaluate the impact of payment modes. Example questions include 'How many specialty admissions occurred last month?' or 'What is the breakdown of admissions by facility?'
[rpt_stock_status_count] Total Stock Status Count — This metric measures the total count of stock statuses across various facilities and product categories. It can be used to analyze inventory levels, identify stock shortages, and assess product availability. Example questions include 'How many stock statuses are reported this month?' and 'What is the stock status count by facility?'. Consider filtering by facility or product category for more granular insights.
[stockout_alerts_count] Stockout Alerts Count — This metric measures the total number of stockout alerts generated within the hospital system. It is useful for tracking medication availability issues and understanding their impact on patient care. Example questions include 'How many stockout alerts were reported last month?' and 'What facilities are experiencing the highest number of stockouts?'. Consider filtering by facility or therapeutic class for more targeted insights.
[theatre_utilization_count] Theatre Utilization Count — This metric measures the total count of theatre utilization sessions within a specified time frame. It is useful for analyzing how effectively theatre resources are being used across different facilities and types. Example questions include 'How many theatre sessions were utilized last month?' or 'What is the utilization count by booking status?'. Consider filtering by facility or theatre type for more granular insights.
[upd_admissions_profile_metrics] Admissions Profile Metrics — This metric provides insights into the number of admissions and their associated costs within the hospital system. Use it to analyze trends in admissions by type, payment mode, and patient demographics such as sex. It can help answer questions like 'What is the average cost of admissions by type?' or 'How many open admissions are there this month?'
[inventory_profile_metrics] Inventory Profile Metrics — This metric provides insights into the total count of inventory items and their lifetime drug costs. Use it to analyze inventory trends over time, assess cost implications, and evaluate the efficiency of drug dispensing. Example questions include 'What is the total count of drugs dispensed this month?' and 'How much have we spent on drugs over their lifetime?'
