[canonical_product_taxonomy_count_metrics] Canonical Product Taxonomy Count Metrics — This metric measures the total count of canonical products and the count of duplicate facilities associated with them. Use this metric to analyze product taxonomy data, identify trends in product categorization, and assess the integrity of facility data. Example questions include 'How many unique canonical products are there?' and 'What is the count of duplicate facilities for these products?'
[doctor_note_terms_count] Count of Doctor Note Terms — This metric measures the total count of doctor note terms recorded in the system. It can be used to analyze trends in clinical documentation, assess the usage of specific terms, and evaluate the status of clinical syndromes and disease burden groups. Example questions include 'How many doctor note terms were recorded last month?' and 'What is the distribution of terms by status?'
[fact_dispensing_metrics] Dispensing Metrics Overview — This metric provides insights into the dispensing activities within the hospital, including total counts, discounts applied, and line totals. Use this metric to analyze dispensing trends, identify stockout events, and evaluate financial impacts. Example questions include 'What is the total number of dispenses this month?' and 'How much discount was given on dispenses last quarter?'
[inpatient_admissions_metrics] Inpatient Admissions Metrics — This metric tracks the total number of inpatient admissions and the total visits count within the hospital system. Use this metric to analyze patient admission trends, evaluate the effectiveness of care, and understand patient demographics based on sex and source of admission. Example questions include 'How many inpatient admissions were there last month?' and 'What is the total visit count for male patients?'
[patient_dispensing_metrics] Patient Dispensing Metrics — This metric tracks the dispensing of medications to patients, including the total number of drugs dispensed, the total cost of these drugs, and counts of unclassified drugs. Use this metric to analyze medication distribution trends over time, assess costs, and identify dispensing patterns. Example questions include 'How many drugs were dispensed last month?' or 'What was the total drug cost for patients in a specific facility?'
[patient_finance_event_metrics] Patient Finance Event Metrics — This metric tracks the count and total amount of financial events related to patients, such as payments and invoices. Use it to analyze financial performance, understand payment trends, and assess the impact of different payment modes. Example questions include 'How many financial events occurred last month?' and 'What was the total amount collected from patient invoices this quarter?'
[patient_invoice_counts] Patient Invoice Counts — This metric measures the total number of patient invoices and the count of events associated with those invoices. It can be used to analyze billing activity over time, identify trends in patient invoicing, and assess the volume of services rendered. Useful questions include 'How many invoices were generated last month?' or 'What is the event count for invoices in a specific facility?'
[ar_aging_count_by_facility_and_bucket] Accounts Receivable Aging Count — This metric measures the count of accounts receivable aging records, categorized by aging bucket and facility. Use this metric to analyze the distribution of outstanding receivables over time, helping to identify trends in collections and outstanding balances. Example questions include 'How many accounts are overdue by 30 days at each facility?' and 'What is the count of receivables in each aging bucket for the last invoice month?'
[bed_occupancy_metrics] Bed Occupancy Metrics — This metric measures the total count of bed occupancy and the average admission cost across different facilities and wards. Use this to analyze trends in bed usage and associated costs over time. Example questions include 'What is the average admission cost for the pediatric ward this month?' or 'How many beds were occupied in the main facility last month?'
[dialysis_session_count] Dialysis Session Count — This metric measures the total number of dialysis sessions conducted within a specified time frame. It can be used to analyze trends in dialysis treatment over time, assess resource allocation, and evaluate facility performance. Example questions include 'How many dialysis sessions were held last month?' or 'What is the session count by facility for the past year?'
[disease_burden_metrics] Disease Burden Metrics — This metric measures the total count of disease cases and the count of prescriptions related to those diseases across different facilities. Use this metric to analyze disease prevalence and treatment patterns over time. Example questions include 'What is the total disease burden for each facility this month?' and 'How many prescriptions were issued for each disease group last month?'
[rpt_dispensing_trends_overview] Dispensing Trends Overview — This metric provides insights into the total number of dispensings and their associated values over time. It can be used to analyze trends in medication dispensing across different facilities and therapeutic classes. Example questions include 'What are the total dispensing values by facility this month?' or 'How many dispensings occurred for each therapeutic class last quarter?'
[rpt_dos_watchlist_count] Count of Watchlist Items — This metric measures the total count of items on the DOS watchlist, providing insights into inventory management and medication monitoring. Use it to answer questions about the number of items flagged for review, track trends over time, or assess the impact of reorder urgency. Important filters include facility and therapeutic class to narrow down specific areas of concern.
[insurance_ar_count_by_facility] Insurance Accounts Receivable Count by Facility — This metric measures the total count of insurance accounts receivable, segmented by facility and insurer. It is useful for analyzing the volume of outstanding insurance claims over time. Example questions include 'How many insurance accounts receivable do we have for each facility this month?' and 'What is the trend in accounts receivable by insurer?'
[kakamega_population_metrics] Kakamega Population Metrics — This metric tracks the total population and visit counts in the Kakamega region. Use it to analyze trends in population and healthcare visits over time, and to answer questions about facility performance and sub-county demographics. Important filters include facility and sub-county to refine your analysis.
[ward_utilisation_metrics] Ward Utilisation Metrics — This metric measures the count and percentage of total utilisation for wards in the Lodwar facility. Use this to analyze how effectively wards are being utilized over time. Example questions include 'What is the total count of patients in each ward?' and 'What percentage of total capacity is being used in the Lodwar facility?'
[procedure_revenue_metrics] Procedure Revenue Metrics — This metric tracks the total count of procedures and the average item amount billed across different facilities and insurers. Use this metric to analyze revenue trends over time, compare performance by facility, or assess the impact of different payment modes. Example questions include 'What is the average revenue per procedure for each facility this month?' or 'How does the procedure count vary by insurer?'
[readmission_metrics] Readmission Metrics — This metric tracks the total number of readmissions and the approximate count of readmissions within 30 days of discharge. Use this data to analyze patient outcomes, evaluate discharge processes, and identify trends in readmission rates. It can help answer questions like 'What is the readmission rate by facility or discharge type?' and 'How do payment modes affect readmission counts?'
[rpt_redistribution_metrics] Redistribution Metrics — This metric tracks the count of redistribution events and the suggested transfer quantities between facilities. Use this to analyze how resources are being allocated, identify deficits and surpluses, and assess clinical priorities. Example questions include 'How many redistribution events occurred last month?' and 'What is the suggested transfer quantity for a specific therapeutic class?'
[specialty_admissions_count] Specialty Admissions Count — This metric measures the total number of specialty admissions within the hospital system. It can be used to analyze trends in admissions over time, assess the performance of different facilities, and evaluate the impact of payment modes. Example questions include 'How many specialty admissions occurred last month?' or 'What is the breakdown of admissions by facility?'
[rpt_stock_status_count] Total Stock Status Count — This metric measures the total count of stock statuses across various facilities and product categories. Use it to analyze inventory levels, identify trends in stock availability, and assess the performance of different therapeutic classes. Example questions include 'What is the total stock status count for a specific facility?' or 'How does the stock status vary by product category?'
[stockout_alerts_count] Stockout Alerts Count — This metric measures the total number of stockout alerts generated within the hospital system. It is useful for tracking medication availability issues and understanding their impact on patient care. Example questions include 'How many stockout alerts were generated last month?' or 'What facilities reported the highest number of stockout alerts?'. Consider filtering by facility or therapeutic class for more specific insights.
[theatre_utilization_count] Theatre Utilization Count — This metric measures the total count of theatre utilization sessions within a specified time frame. It can be used to analyze how effectively theatre resources are being used across different facilities and types. Example questions include 'How many sessions were booked in the main theatre last month?' or 'What is the utilization count for each booking status?'. Filters can be applied based on facility, theatre name, and booking status for more granular insights.
[upd_admissions_profile_metrics] Admissions Profile Metrics — This metric provides insights into the number of admissions and their associated costs within the hospital system. It can be used to analyze trends in admissions by type, payment mode, and patient demographics such as sex. Example questions include 'What is the total admission cost for open admissions this month?' and 'How many admissions were recorded by type in the last quarter?'
[inventory_profile_metrics] Inventory Profile Metrics — This metric provides insights into the inventory profile of drugs, measuring the total count of items and their lifetime drug cost. Use this metric to analyze drug availability and financial impact over time. Example questions include 'What is the total count of drugs dispensed this month?' and 'How much have we spent on drugs in the last quarter?'
