[rpt_dispensing_trends_overview] Dispensing Trends Overview — This metric provides insights into the total number of dispensings and their associated values over time. It can be used to analyze trends in medication dispensing across different facilities and therapeutic classes. Example questions include 'What are the total dispensing values by facility this month?' and 'How many dispensings occurred in the last quarter for a specific therapeutic class?'
[rpt_dos_watchlist_count] Count of Watchlist Items — This metric measures the total count of items on the DOS watchlist, providing insights into inventory management and medication monitoring. Use this metric to answer questions about the number of items flagged for review, track trends over time, or assess the impact of reorder urgency. Important filters include facility and therapeutic class to narrow down specific areas of concern.
[insurance_ar_count_by_facility] Insurance Accounts Receivable Count by Facility — This metric measures the total count of insurance accounts receivable, segmented by facility and insurer. It is useful for analyzing the volume of outstanding insurance claims over time. Example questions include 'How many insurance accounts receivable do we have for each facility this month?' and 'What is the trend in accounts receivable by insurer? Be sure to filter by invoice month for specific time periods.
[kakamega_population_metrics] Kakamega Population Metrics — This metric tracks the total population and visit counts in the Kakamega region. Use it to analyze trends in population and healthcare visits over time, and to answer questions about facility performance and sub-county demographics. Important filters include facility and sub-county to refine your analysis.
[ward_utilisation_metrics] Ward Utilisation Metrics — This metric measures the count and percentage of total utilisation for wards in the Lodwar facility. Use this to analyze how effectively wards are being utilized over time. Example questions include 'What is the total count of patients in each ward?' and 'What percentage of total capacity is being used in the Lodwar facility?'.
[procedure_revenue_metrics] Procedure Revenue Metrics — This metric tracks the total count of procedures and the average item amount billed across different facilities and insurers. Use it to analyze revenue trends over time, compare performance by facility, or assess the impact of different payment modes. Example questions include 'What is the average revenue per procedure for each facility this month?' or 'How does the procedure count vary by insurer?'
[readmission_metrics] Readmission Metrics — This metric tracks the total number of readmissions and the approximate count of readmissions within 30 days of discharge. Use this data to analyze patient outcomes, evaluate discharge processes, and identify trends in readmission rates. It can help answer questions like 'What is the readmission rate by facility or discharge type?' and 'How do payment modes affect readmission counts?'
[rpt_redistribution_transfer_metrics] Redistribution Transfer Metrics — This metric tracks the count of redistribution events and the suggested transfer quantities between facilities. Use this to analyze how resources are being allocated, identify deficits and surpluses, and assess clinical priorities. Example questions include 'How many transfers were suggested last month?' and 'What is the total suggested transfer quantity for high-priority cases?'
