WARNING 2026-07-29 09:42:13,272 nodes 4063372 131970537334464 catalog_text: [canonical_keys_count] Count of Canonical Keys — This metric measures the total count of canonical keys in the system. It can be used to analyze the distribution of different therapeutic classes and subclasses, as well as the strength and form of the canonical names. Example questions include 'How many canonical keys are there for each therapeutic class?' and 'What is the count of canonical keys by form type?'.
[canonical_product_taxonomy_count_metrics] Canonical Product Taxonomy Count Metrics — This metric measures the total count of canonical products and the count of facility duplicates within the product taxonomy. Use this metric to analyze product distribution across facilities, identify duplicate entries, and assess the completeness of product data. Example questions include 'How many unique products are there?' and 'What is the count of duplicates by facility?'
[doctor_note_terms_count] Count of Doctor Note Terms — This metric measures the total count of doctor note terms recorded in the system. It can be used to analyze the frequency of specific terms, clinical syndromes, or disease burden groups in patient notes. Example questions include 'How many times has a specific term been used?' or 'What is the distribution of terms by status?'. Consider filtering by clinical syndrome or status for more targeted insights.
[fact_dispensing_metrics] Dispensing Metrics Overview — This metric provides insights into the dispensing activities within the hospital, including total counts, discounts applied, and line totals. Use this metric to analyze dispensing trends, identify stockout events, and evaluate financial impacts. Example questions include 'What is the total number of dispenses this month?' and 'How much discount was applied to dispenses in the last quarter?'
[inpatient_admissions_metrics] Inpatient Admissions Metrics — This metric tracks the total number of inpatient admissions and the total visits count within the hospital system. Use this metric to analyze patient admission trends, evaluate the effectiveness of healthcare services, and understand patient demographics based on sex and source of admission. It can help answer questions like 'How many patients were admitted last month?' or 'What is the total visit count for male patients?'
[patient_dispensing_metrics] Patient Dispensing Metrics — This metric tracks the dispensing of medications to patients, including the total number of drugs dispensed, the total cost of drugs, and counts of unclassified drugs. Use this metric to analyze medication distribution trends over time, assess costs, and identify dispensing patterns. Example questions include 'How many drugs were dispensed last month?' or 'What was the total drug cost for patients in a specific facility?'
[patient_finance_event_metrics] Patient Finance Event Metrics — This metric tracks the count and total amount of financial events related to patients, such as payments and invoices. Use this metric to analyze financial performance, identify trends in patient payments, and assess the effectiveness of different payment modes. Example questions include 'What is the total amount collected this month?' or 'How many finance events occurred for a specific patient?'.
[patient_invoice_counts] Patient Invoice Counts — This metric measures the total number of patient invoices and the count of events associated with those invoices. Use it to analyze billing activity over time, identify trends in patient invoicing, and assess the volume of services rendered. Example questions include 'How many invoices were generated last month?' and 'What is the event count for invoices in a specific facility?'
[ar_aging_count_by_facility] Accounts Receivable Aging Count by Facility — This metric measures the count of accounts receivable aging records, categorized by facility and aging bucket. Use it to analyze the distribution of outstanding invoices across different facilities and insurers over time. Example questions include 'How many aging accounts do we have at each facility this month?' and 'What is the count of invoices in each aging bucket for a specific insurer?'
[bed_occupancy_metrics] Bed Occupancy Metrics — This metric measures the total count of bed occupancy and the average admission cost across different facilities and wards. Use this metric to analyze trends in bed usage and associated costs over time. Example questions include 'What is the average admission cost per facility?' or 'How does bed occupancy vary by ward age group?'
[dialysis_session_count] Dialysis Session Count — This metric measures the total number of dialysis sessions conducted within a specified time frame. It can be used to analyze trends in dialysis treatment over time, assess resource allocation, and identify peak usage periods. Example questions include 'How many dialysis sessions were held last month?' or 'What is the session count by facility for the past year?'
[disease_burden_metrics] Disease Burden Metrics — This metric measures the total count of disease cases and the count of prescriptions related to those diseases across different facilities. Use this metric to analyze disease prevalence and treatment patterns over time. Example questions include 'What is the total disease burden for a specific disease group this month?' and 'How many prescriptions were issued for each disease group at our facilities?'
[rpt_dispensing_trends_overview] Dispensing Trends Overview — This metric provides insights into the total number of dispensings and their associated values over time. It can be used to analyze trends in medication dispensing across different facilities and therapeutic classes. Example questions include 'What are the total dispensing values by facility this month?' and 'How many dispensings occurred in the last quarter for a specific therapeutic class?'
[rpt_dos_watchlist_count] Count of Watchlist Items — This metric measures the total count of items on the DOS watchlist, providing insights into inventory management and medication monitoring. Use this metric to answer questions about the number of items flagged for review, track trends over time, or assess the impact of reorder urgency. Important filters include facility and therapeutic class to narrow down specific areas of concern.
[insurance_ar_count_by_facility] Insurance Accounts Receivable Count by Facility — This metric measures the total count of insurance accounts receivable, segmented by facility and insurer. It is useful for analyzing the volume of outstanding insurance claims over time. Example questions include 'How many insurance accounts receivable do we have for each facility this month?' and 'What is the trend in accounts receivable by insurer? Be sure to filter by invoice month for specific time periods.
[kakamega_population_metrics] Kakamega Population Metrics — This metric tracks the total population and visit counts in the Kakamega region. Use it to analyze trends in population and healthcare visits over time, and to answer questions about facility performance and sub-county demographics. Important filters include facility and sub-county to refine your analysis.
[ward_utilisation_metrics] Ward Utilisation Metrics — This metric measures the count and percentage of total utilisation for wards in the Lodwar facility. Use this to analyze how effectively wards are being utilized over time. Example questions include 'What is the total count of patients in each ward?' and 'What percentage of total capacity is being used in the Lodwar facility?'.
[procedure_revenue_metrics] Procedure Revenue Metrics — This metric tracks the total count of procedures and the average item amount billed across different facilities and insurers. Use it to analyze revenue trends over time, compare performance by facility, or assess the impact of different payment modes. Example questions include 'What is the average revenue per procedure for each facility this month?' or 'How does the procedure count vary by insurer?'
[readmission_metrics] Readmission Metrics — This metric tracks the total number of readmissions and the approximate count of readmissions within 30 days of discharge. Use this data to analyze patient outcomes, evaluate discharge processes, and identify trends in readmission rates. It can help answer questions like 'What is the readmission rate by facility or discharge type?' and 'How do payment modes affect readmission counts?'
[rpt_redistribution_transfer_metrics] Redistribution Transfer Metrics — This metric tracks the count of redistribution events and the suggested transfer quantities between facilities. Use this to analyze how resources are being allocated, identify deficits and surpluses, and assess clinical priorities. Example questions include 'How many transfers were suggested last month?' and 'What is the total suggested transfer quantity for high-priority cases?'
[specialty_admissions_count] Specialty Admissions Count — This metric measures the total number of specialty admissions to the hospital. It can be used to analyze trends in admissions over time, assess the impact of different payment modes, and evaluate performance across various facilities and wards. Example questions include 'How many specialty admissions occurred last month?' and 'What is the breakdown of admissions by payment mode?'
[rpt_stock_status_count] Total Stock Status Count — This metric measures the total count of stock statuses across various facilities and product categories. It can be used to analyze inventory levels, track stock availability, and identify trends in product usage. Example questions include 'What is the total stock status count for a specific facility?' or 'How many products are currently in stock by category?'.
[stockout_alerts_count] Stockout Alerts Count — This metric measures the total number of stockout alerts generated within the hospital system. It is useful for tracking medication availability issues and understanding their impact on patient care. Example questions include 'How many stockout alerts were reported last month?' and 'What facilities are experiencing the highest number of stockouts?'. Consider filtering by facility or therapeutic class for more targeted insights.
[theatre_utilization_count] Theatre Utilization Count — This metric measures the total count of theatre utilization sessions, providing insights into how often theatres are booked and used. It can help answer questions about booking trends, facility performance, and session frequency. Use filters like booking status, facility, and theatre type to refine your analysis.
[upd_admissions_profile_metrics] Admissions Profile Metrics — This metric provides insights into the number of admissions and their associated costs within the hospital system. It can be used to analyze trends in admissions by type, payment mode, and patient demographics such as sex. Example questions include 'What is the total admission count for open admissions this month?' and 'How do admission costs vary by admission type?'.
[inventory_profile_metrics] Inventory Profile Metrics — This metric provides insights into the inventory profile of drugs, measuring the total count of items and their lifetime drug cost. Use this metric to analyze drug inventory trends, assess cost implications, and evaluate the efficiency of drug dispensation over time. Example questions include 'What is the total count of drugs dispensed this month?' and 'How much has been spent on drugs in the last quarter?'
